source: packages/tier1/dist/tests/distributions.rs
expression: all
---
error[Z0413]: `p` of `quantile` must be a probability between 0 and 1, but this is 1.5
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:24
  |
1 | dist.normal().quantile(1.5)
  |                        ^^^ not a probability

error[Z0413]: `p` of `quantile` must be a probability between 0 and 1, but this is -0.1
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:24
  |
1 | dist.normal().quantile(-0.1)
  |                        ^^^^ not a probability

error[Z0413]: `max` of `dist.uniform` must exceed `min`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:27
  |
1 | dist.uniform(min: 3, max: 1)
  |                           ^ outside the parameter's domain
  |
  = help: `zeff help dist.uniform` gives the domain of every parameter

error[Z0413]: `sdlog` of `dist.lognormal` must be a positive number, but this is -1
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:23
  |
1 | dist.lognormal(sdlog: -1)
  |                       ^^ outside the parameter's domain
  |
  = help: `zeff help dist.lognormal` gives the domain of every parameter

error[Z0413]: `rate` of `dist.exponential` must be a positive number, but this is 0
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:24
  |
1 | dist.exponential(rate: 0)
  |                        ^ outside the parameter's domain
  |
  = help: `zeff help dist.exponential` gives the domain of every parameter

error[Z0401]: `n` of `draw` must be 0 or more, but this is -1
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:20
  |
1 | dist.normal().draw(-1)
  |                    ^^ a negative count

error[Z0401]: `n` of `draw` must be an Int, but this is a Float
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:20
  |
1 | dist.normal().draw(2.5)
  |                    ^^^ a Float
  |
  = help: usage: `distribution.draw(n, seed: Int)`

error[Z0401]: `seed` of `draw` must be an Int, but this is a Float
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:29
  |
1 | dist.normal().draw(3, seed: 1.5)
  |                             ^^^ a Float
  |
  = help: usage: `distribution.draw(n, seed: Int)`

error[Z0401]: `x` of `cdf` must be a Float, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:19
  |
1 | dist.normal().cdf("x")
  |                   ^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: usage: `distribution.cdf(x, upper: Bool = false)`
